WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.630
Though they have years of experience under
their belts, our MCU favorites aren't immune

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.360
to making mistakes on the job. Such is the
case for the cast of Avengers: Endgame, who

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.590
goofed up a handful of times while filming
the superhero blockbuster. Here are some of

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:14.740
our favorite Endgame bloopers and outtakes.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.260
Oh, Chris Pratt. Arguably the goofiest of
the three Chrises in the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:23.280
Universe, the charismatic guy who plays Star-Lord
is known for getting the giggles going on

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.880
set — even in a movie with as much emotion
and intensity as Endgame. While preparing

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.980
to face off against Thanos in the film's epic
third act, Pratt offers a hilarious piece

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.420
of advice to keep the actors safe during shooting.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:39.140
"Nobody pull a hamstring! Warm your butt cheeks
up. Warm up your butt cheeks!"

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.679
Later in the Endgame blooper reel, Pratt provides
more laughs when he stops to fix his hair

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.680
between takes.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.220
Fat Thor, officially known as "Bro Thor,"
was a prominent part of Endgame, with many

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:53.699
arguing about the purpose and potential negative
consequences of portraying the God of Thunder

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:57.750
with a plumper physique, an increased love
for beer and candy, and a gloomier outlook

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.890
on life. It turns out that sticking ripped
Aussie actor Chris Hemsworth in a fat suit

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:06.170
and a bunch of heavy prosthetics allowed for
many antics to happen while shooting Endgame,

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:08.540
including this fun moment with a Rocket Racoon
stand-in ...

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:17.500
Robert Downey Jr. is the focus of many Endgame
bloopers, starting with the slip-up that occurred

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.500
when he was filming a scene at the S.H.I.E.L.D.
base in the 1970s while attempting to get

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.060
his hands on the Tesseract after the Avengers
failed to retrieve it from 2012 New York.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.860
Everything goes mostly according to plan,
with Tony Stark and Steve Rogers doing their

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:34.171
best to blend in and complete their high-stakes
mission. Tony ends up making his way to the

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:39.080
Tesseract, snagging it, sticking it in his
briefcase, and heading back to the year 2023

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.940
to load up the Avengers' Infinity Gauntlet
and bring back the billions of people Thanos

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:43.440
dusted.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:47.920
In one take of the scene in which Tony retrieves
the Tesseract, Downey Jr. reaches out to grab

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.710
the glowing blue cube that holds the Space
Stone… and then pulls a little too hard

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:53.700
"I broke it."

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.740
Scarlet Witch actress Elizabeth Olsen took
a tumble on set as she shot the heroine's

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.840
vengeance-tinged sequence at the end of the
film. The moment happened while Olsen's Scarlet

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.840
Witch was making her way toward Thanos to
unleash the full capacity of her mystical

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.069
powers and give him a piece of her mind. The
theatrical version of that scene was impactful

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:15.300
enough to send shivers down every viewers'
spines, but one take saw Olsen slip and fall

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.980
before she could reach the Mad Titan.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.200
The time travel in Avengers: Endgame is difficult
to wrap your head around. Paul Rudd, whose

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:28.659
superhero character Ant-Man knows plenty about
time travel, alternate dimensions and how

00:02:28.659 --> 00:02:32.499
to navigate the Quantum Realm, got a bit flustered
while trying to explain the rules of time

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.230
travel as outlined in Endgame.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.440
"The thing about time travel…"

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.450
In another Endgame outtake, Captain America
actor Chris Evans laughs over the mask he

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.900
wore in 2012's Avengers, which he apparently
now thinks is dorky or maybe uncomfortable.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.440
"I can't believe I made a whole movie with
this thing on.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:55.180
In another blooper, Captain Marvel star Brie
Larson admits that she doesn't feel cool while

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:59.100
wearing a bald cap and hanging from a harness
for a scene in which her character is flying.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:03.499
“Yeah. Does it look cool, or? It doesn't
feel cool, but if it looks cool, that's what

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.500
matters."

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:09.420
Shooting a film as monumental as Avengers:
Endgame works up a mighty appetite, and the

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.500
stars were apparently thinking of snacks and
sugary sodas while on set.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.100
"Do you have any idea what's coursing through
my veins right now?"

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.100
"Funyuns?"

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:21.320
"Yes!"

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.180
Another Endgame blooper shows Ancient One
portrayer Tilda Swinton asking for an orange

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:31.040
soda while shooting. Right on cue, up pops
a hand with a glass bottle of the fizzy stuff.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.420
Thanos wasn't the only enemy Tony Stark had
to face off against in Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:39.720
Actor Robert Downey Jr. faced some trouble
with the automatic trunk of Tony's sleek sports

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:43.090
car while trying to shut it before heading
into Avengers HQ.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:48.220
"We are getting the whole team, aren't we?
F---a duck!"

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.519
From losing his wife and children in Thanos'
Decimation at the start of the film to taking

00:03:57.519 --> 00:04:01.950
on the moniker Ronin and going on a revenge-fueled
killing spree and watching his fellow Avenger

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:06.280
Black Widow die in front of his eyes, Hawkeye
had a dark storyline in Avengers: Endgame.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.120
However, the actor who plays the sharp-shooting
hero had a lot of fun on set.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:22.220
The Endgame blooper reel ends just as the
Infinity Saga did: with Iron Man. Actor Robert

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:26.349
Downey Jr. is the last face fans see in the
collection of goof-ups, shown shooting the

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:30.379
scene in which he returns to 2012 New York.
Part of that portion of the Avengers' time

00:04:30.379 --> 00:04:35.310
heist mission involved Tony Stark disguising
himself as a law enforcement officer responding

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:39.552
to the chaos in Stark Tower. While filming
that sequence, Downey Jr. jokes that every

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:43.440
take he's delivered has been flawless and
that he simply can't improve upon perfection:

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:48.100
We know RDJ is just being silly, but there's
some truth to his quip. His Iron Man was the

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:52.510
hero who laid the foundation for the MCU,
and without him, the Marvel movie world wouldn't

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:53.380
be what it is today.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.540
"I feel like I've given you all you could
ever want."

